                "Match the test to the assumption. Common test types: prototype tests (usability and comprehension), one-question surveys in context, data mining of existing behaviour, fake door or painted door tests (a button for a feature that doesn't exist yet, measuring clicks, followed by an honest message), concierge tests (deliver the value manually), and Wizard of Oz tests (the user sees a product, a human does the work behind it). Since 2025 many PMs build working prototypes with AI coding tools in hours, which makes value and usability tests far cheaper, but a convincing prototype is not evidence of feasibility at scale.",
